### Phase 4 — Baseline Modelling: Logistic Regression
**Owner:** Inês + Mariana · **Report section:** Methodology — Baseline (~0.75 pages)

- [ ] **Preprocessing pipeline:**
  - One-hot encode categorical variables (Education, Marital_Status)
  - Standard scale numerical features (required for Logistic Regression)
  - Train/test split: 80/20, **stratified** on `Response`
- [ ] **Train Logistic Regression:**
  - Default settings first, then apply regularization
  - Try L1 (Lasso — implicit feature selection) and L2 (Ridge)
  - Use `class_weight='balanced'` to handle class imbalance
- [ ] **Cross-validation:** 5-fold stratified CV, report mean AUC
- [ ] **Hyperparameter tuning:** GridSearchCV on `C` (regularization strength)
- [ ] **Evaluation metrics:**
  - **ROC-AUC** ← primary metric (we rank customers by probability, not just classify)
  - Precision, Recall, F1 (Recall is especially important — we don't want to miss buyers)
  - Confusion Matrix
- [ ] Write baseline modelling section of the report

> 💡 **Why AUC?** A campaign manager wants to target the top 20% most likely to respond. AUC measures the model's ability to rank customers correctly, regardless of a fixed threshold.

